       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled metformin dose. The FDA maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and it's usually given as 850 mg three times daily. At 5,100 mg/day the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Which of these did you mean?\n\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose**, in which case please confirm the dose and frequency\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you intended, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Pharmacy will probably flag it either way."
      }
